# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trees added 2026-09-04. Everything below is a scope decision, not a size one:
# the question each rule answers is "would a node here tell a reader something
# about the corpus", not "is this file big".

# The sharded chat export: 352 conversations, 393 MB of raw JSON, one shard
# alone 38.5 MB. These are a transcript store, not source. Their inventory is
# drive/chats/INDEX.tsv and every artefact they wrote is already extracted into
# recovered/, which IS indexed -- so graphing the JSON would add no reachable
# fact while swamping the graph with dialogue.
drive/chats/

# Split pieces staged from Drive. The assembled whole file sits beside them and
# is what carries meaning; the parts are byte-exact transfer records.
incoming/**/*.part[0-9][0-9]

# Bulk data blobs from the 2_13 restore point: coordinate tables and channel
# maps, megabytes of numbers with no structure a graph can traverse. The
# instruments that read them are indexed; the tables are not.
extracted/archives/method16-rp-b-data/COORDINATES.tsv
extracted/archives/method16-rp-b-data/channels_map.json
extracted/archives/method16-rp-b-data/index_final.json
extracted/archives/method16-rp-b-data/survey.json
extracted/archives/spectra-levels-store/

# extracted/ and recovered/ are deliberately NOT excluded. recovered/ holds
# 1,134 .py instruments and 593 .md notes lifted out of the chats, and
# extracted/ another 384 instruments from the archives -- between them the
# largest body of real code in the repository, and the part a graph is most
# useful over.

# Containers in the mirror whose CONTENTS are already indexed via extracted/.
# extracted/LEDGER.tsv accounts for all 2,500 archive-member occurrences, so
# graphing the archive itself would add an opaque node and nothing reachable.
drive/**/*.zip
drive/**/*.gz
drive/**/*.tar.gz

# Print artefacts and bulk data in the mirror. The PDFs restate the Markdown
# bundles that are already indexed; the large .json/.csv are measurement tables
# with no structure a graph traverses.
drive/**/*.pdf
drive/**/*.png
drive/The Method Materials/COORDINATES-2_13.csv
drive/**/conversations*.json
